<newsitem itemid="65588" id="root" date="1996-09-19" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Geest half year pretax profit slips.</title>
<headline>Geest half year pretax profit slips.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ending June 29</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		6.9		    vs 8.2</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 3.7		    vs 3.7</p>
<p> Pretax		     7.3		    vs 9.0</p>
<p> Turnover		   207.3		  vs 191.1</p>
<p> Operating result	 3.3		    vs 11.7</p>
<p> Exceptional		15.4 income	  vs 4.5 charge</p>
<p> Interest		   0.9 income	   vs 3.7 charge</p>
<p> Tax			  2.0 charge	   vs 2.9 charge</p>
<p> Net taxed		  20.7		   vs 1.1</p>
<p> Pay date		   December 27</p>
<p> Div registration date  November 26</p>
<p> Ex-div date		November 18</p>
<p>Note - Food group Geest Plc said the exceptional income of 15.4 million stg came from 18.2 million stg profit on sale of its banana business and an exceptional charge of 2.8 million stg for restructuring its imported whole produce business.</p>
<p>Geest said in a statement the year so far had &quot;more than met our expectations&quot;, adding that it had &quot;confidence both in the outcome for 1996 and the future of Geest&quot;.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 5427717</p>
</text>
